From 5da68b32e9495eb64846bb3ea195d432f360eb9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:01:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Copilot: refused proposals explain themselves, one repair
 round, real default values
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bug: asked to start Q2 at 19, the model proposed a sandboxed script that
set the input's value and dispatched DOM events. The Studio refused it, the
proposal had nothing left to apply, and the card showed a disabled Apply with
no reason (its tooltip even said "Apply as one undoable change").

- The card lists refused actions with their reasons; Apply's tooltip says when
  there is nothing to apply. diffSurveys counts default-value and custom-HTML
  changes, so a proposal of only those is no longer "empty".
- The turn route sends refusals back to the model once and uses the corrected
  answer when the Studio accepts more of it; the card says a correction happened.
- settings.defaultValue (Properties → Default / piped value) now works at
  runtime: filled in when the question is first shown, only if unanswered, once;
  numbers for numeric, codes for choice questions, piping resolved.
- New look-only copilot action set_default_value, gated against the question.
- Scripts that try to fill in answers are refused with a pointer to the default
  value; page_enter/select_option… are accepted as rs.listen aliases.
- Tests: engine defaultValue.test.ts, studio copilot.test.ts, browser
  default-value-test.mjs; copilot-test asserts the card's refusal note. All
  mutation-checked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAcfUsJLu3R4pYxzaj9SU4
